WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000 line:100%,end
Parts stock has two buttons:
Scan · Stock in and Scan · Stock out.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000 line:100%,end
The administrator opens Stock in.
Read the barcode with the camera, or type the code.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000 line:100%,end
An unknown code can be linked to an existing part,
or a new part can be created from it.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000 line:100%,end
When the part is found, the quantity is already 1.
Type the shelf location. The other fields are optional.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:31.000 line:100%,end
Press Save.
The movement is stored: direction, quantity, person and time.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000 line:100%,end
Stock in was saved.
The balance rises by the quantity stored.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.000 line:100%,end
Stock out works for maintenance as well.
Read the code and type the quantity.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:49.000 line:100%,end
If needed, choose a machine or an open work order.
Then press Save.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:56.000 line:100%,end
The balance never falls below zero.
If there is not enough of the part, you see this notice.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000 line:100%,end
Stock out was saved.
The balance drops by the quantity taken.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:09.000 line:100%,end
On the part page, Movements shows the history.
Filter by direction and date.
